{"url": "https://chem.washington.edu/phd-student-financial-support", "final_url": "https://chem.washington.edu/phd-student-financial-support", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-23", "text": "Ph.D. Student Financial Support | Department of Chemistry | University of Washington\nSkip to main content\nCollege of Arts & Sciences\nQuick links\nQuick Links\nMake a Gift\nDirectories\nMaps\nMyUW\nUser account menu\nSearch\nSearch\nGive now\nMain menu\nDepartment of Chemistry\nMenu\nPeople\nFull Directory\nFaculty\nDepartment Faculty\nAdjuncts & Affiliates\nEmeriti Faculty\nIn Memoriam\nPostdoctoral Scholars\nStaff\nVisitors\nAlumni\nAlumni News\nSubmit an Update\nPrograms & Courses\nUndergraduate\nAdvising & Academic Support\nAdmissions\nMajor & Minor Requirements\nGraduation Information\nRegistration & Course Selection\nResources & Opportunities\nResearch & Careers\nLearning Strategies\nGraduate\nAdmissions\nMaster's Program\nPh.D. Program\nStudent Community\nCourses\nUpcoming Courses\nCourse Materials & Syllabi\nChoosing Introductory Courses\nChoosing Organic Courses\nChoosing Advanced Electives\nDuplication Guidelines\nAdd/Drop Class\nLab Information\n1xx Series: Introductory Chemistry\n2xx/3xx Series: Organic Chemistry\nResearch\nResearch Areas\nCenters & Institutes\nComputing Resources\nTraining Opportunities\nResearch News\nNews & Events\nRecent News\nNewsletter\nCalendar\nEndowed Lectures\nResources\nAdvising\nEducation\nStudy Centers\nTeaching & Learning\nLecture Demos\nStudent Organizations\nCommunity Resources\nFacilities\nNMR\nMass Spectrometry\nCore Instrumentation\nX-Ray Crystallography\nPhotonics Research Center\nInstrument Reservations\nServices\nResearch Stockroom\nComputing Support\nElectronics Shop\nMachine Shop\nHealth & Safety\nAccident Reporting & Prevention\nBuildings & Labs\nChemical Database\nNew Employee Safety Orientation\nDepartmental Users\nPolicies & Procedures\nPurchasing & Accounting\nProposal Preparation\nInstructor Information\nTA Information\nInternal Resources\nFaculty Meetings: Agenda & Minutes\nChemistry Sharepoint\nAbout\nDepartment Profile\nInclusive Chemistry\nEmployment\nStay Connected\nSupport Us\nContact Us\nMake a Gift\nDirectories\nMaps\nMyUW\nYou are here\nHome\nPrograms & Courses\nGraduate\nPh.D. Program\nProspective Students\nPh.D. Student Financial Support\nMost PhD students are supported throughout the year (including summer) by teaching and research assistantships. TAs and RAs receive a competitive salary, a full tuition waiver, and a comprehensive medical/dental/vision plan (free to the student; 50% premium for dependents). A modest student activities fee is paid by students each quarter.\nTeaching Assistantships\nNew graduate students are awarded teaching assistantships. These offer students an opportunity to gain teaching experience at the college level, to sharpen their understanding of fundamental chemical concepts, and to practice presenting technical material to a group. Graduate students often find teaching to be among the most meaningful experiences of their doctoral training.\nResearch Assistantships\nFunds for research assistantships come from research grants awarded to individual faculty members and provide support for research in defined areas. Graduate students are often appointed to a research assistantship after formal acceptance into a research group.\nIndependent Fellowships\nSome graduate students are independently awarded fellowships from funding agencies, such as the National Science Foundation\u2019s Graduate Research Fellowship Program (NSF GRFP). For students who are applying to the NSF GRFP, the Department of Chemistry offers a writing course with feedback from peers and faculty mentors.\nPredoctoral Instructors\nStudents who have demonstrated outstanding teaching ability may be offered the opportunity to have complete responsibility for an undergraduate course, with a concomitant increase in salary. This may be of special interest to students considering an academic career.\nShare\nPrograms & Courses\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nAdmissions\nMaster's Program\nPh.D. Program\nProspective Students\nApplication Instructions\nFinancial Support\nCurrent Students\nStudent Community\nCourses\n1xx Series: Introductory Chemistry\n2xx/3xx Series: Organic Chemistry\nSupport Chemistry\nFacebook\nTwitter\nNewsletter\nNews Feed\nDepartment of Chemistry\nUniversity of Washington\n109 Bagley Hall\nBox 351700\nSeattle, WA 98195-1700\nMain Office: 206.543.1610\nchemdesk@uw.edu\nAdvising: 206.616.9880\nchemadv@uw.edu\nPrivacy\nTerms\nSite Map\nAlumni Update\nContact Us\n\u00a9 2026 University of Washington. All rights reserved.", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://chem.washington.edu/phd-student-financial-support#main-content"], ["Washington University of Washington", "https://www.washington.edu"], ["College of Arts & Sciences", "https://artsci.washington.edu"], ["Make a Gift", "https://chem.washington.edu/support-us"], ["Directories", "https://uw.edu/directory"], ["Maps", "https://uw.edu/maps"], ["MyUW", "https://my.uw.edu"], ["", "https://chem.washington.edu/saml/login?destination=/phd-student-financial-support"], ["Search", "https://chem.washington.edu/phd-student-financial-support"], ["Give now", "https://chem.washington.edu/support-us"], ["Department of Chemistry", "https://chem.washington.edu/"], ["Menu", "https://chem.washington.edu/phd-student-financial-support"], ["People", "https://chem.washington.edu/people"], ["Full Directory", "https://chem.washington.edu/people"], ["Faculty", "https://chem.washington.edu/people/faculty"], ["Department Faculty", "https://chem.washington.edu/people/faculty"], ["Adjuncts & Affiliates", "https://chem.washington.edu/people/adjuncts-affiliates"], ["Emeriti Faculty", "https://chem.washington.edu/people/emeriti"], ["In Memoriam", "https://chem.washington.edu/people/in-memoriam"], ["Postdoctoral Scholars", "https://chem.washington.edu/people/postdoc"], ["Staff", "https://chem.wa